---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import DemoBanner from "../components/DemoBanner.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology — Is Poland Safe Now?"
  description="How Is Poland Safe Now? classifies regional security status: current demonstration-data phase and the planned news-collection and AI-assisted classification pipeline."
  path="/methodology"
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <DemoBanner />
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-6 px-4 py-8 text-slate-700">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Methodology</h1>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Current phase: demonstration data</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        This build ships only the site foundation: the interactive map, homepage, region pages, and a public API,
        all backed by fixed demonstration classifications. No news collection or AI classification runs yet. Every
        status shown is a hand-authored example value, clearly labeled as demonstration data throughout the site.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Status levels</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Green</strong> — no elevated regional signal found.</li>
        <li><strong>Yellow</strong> — elevated situation requiring attention.</li>
        <li><strong>Red</strong> — serious active warning or confirmed incident.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Unknown</strong> — missing, stale, conflicting, or insufficient information. Missing data always
          resolves to Unknown, never Green.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Planned pipeline (not yet implemented)</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        The production system will later collect news from public sources relevant to Poland's security situation
        (the Russia-Ukraine war, Belarus border activity, Kaliningrad, airspace violations, drone or missile
        incidents, RCB warnings, and transport disruptions), and send that evidence to TypeSafe AI for
        region-by-region classification. Classifications will be re-run on a schedule and stored with full
        evidence trails in the database, following the same <code>ClassificationService</code> interface this phase
        already defines.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Map data</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Voivodeship boundaries are sourced from Poland's official geospatial registry (GUGiK PRG) and converted to a
        local SVG at development time — see
        <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/pvgomes/ispolandsafenow/blob/main/DATA_SOURCES.md">
          DATA_SOURCES.md
        </a>
        in the repository for the full attribution and license.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Limits</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        This is an independent information service, not an official warning system, and cannot guarantee safety.
        Always follow instructions from Polish authorities and RCB. For emergencies, call 112.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
